 # Living Survey: Artificial_General_Intelligence                                                              
                                                                                                               
 ## Introduction                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
 This document collects the scientific literature regarding **Artificial_General_Intelligence**.               
+                                                                                                              
+## Policy and Ethical Implications                                                                            
+                                                                                                              
+Recent policy discussions in the European Union have highlighted the need for conceptual discipline when      
addressing Artificial General Intelligence (AGI) in healthcare. The authors argue that the term AGI is         
contested and potentially risky, suggesting that its use in funding calls may conflict with established        
precautionary principles. This underscores the growing tension between rapid technological advancement and     
regulatory frameworks [^10.1016_j.jrt.2026.100183].                                                            
+                                                                                                              
+Critical analysis of the AGI development movement reveals deep normative roots in the Anglo-American eugenics 
tradition. The authors argue that framing AGI as an unquestioned goal for "safety" and "benefiting humanity"   
masks discriminatory attitudes that could centralize power and harm marginalized groups. This perspective urges
a shift toward developing defined, testable systems rather than pursuing an all-knowing AGI                    
[^10.5210_fm.v29i4.13636].                                                                                     
+                                                                                                              
+## Cognitive Architectures and Consciousness                                                                  
+                                                                                                              
+This work proposes a foundational shift in cognitive science by replacing the subjective unit with a "Form F" 
to describe the transition from computation to autonomy. It frames consciousness as the systemic capacity to   
integrate stochastic perturbations into a stable gradient, mathematically linking autonomy and survival        
instincts to the preservation of topological integrity. This approach establishes a rigorous geometric         
framework for understanding the emergence of AGI [^10.5281_zenodo.19034234].                                   
+                                                                                                              
+The intersection of logic, metamathematics, and brain sciences has renewed interest in artificial             
consciousness. This paper explores conjectures regarding sufficiently advanced general robotic intelligence,   
questioning whether it would be indistinguishable from human consciousness. It further examines the            
implications of such systems in responsible roles and their relationship to broader theories of mind,          
emergence, and free will [^10.22339_jbh.v7i4.7403].                                                            
+                                                                                                              
+## Safety and Verification                                                                                    
+                                                                                                              
+This paper outlines a pathway to safely deploying powerful AGIs by ensuring they provably satisfy             
human-specified requirements. It argues that advanced AI for formal verification and mechanistic               
interpretability will soon make this technically feasible, presenting it as the only guaranteed path to        
controllable AGI. The authors propose a set of challenge problems to advance this critical safety research     
[^10.48550_arxiv.2309.01933].                                                                                  
+                                                                                                              
+## Geopolitical Strategies                                                                                    
+                                                                                                              
+China's national strategy explicitly targets leadership in "general AI" capable of autonomous action in novel 
circumstances by 2030. Open-source research identifies numerous institutions engaged in machine learning,      
brain-inspired AI, and brain-computer interfaces. This report highlights the geopolitical race to achieve AGI  
and the mechanisms in place to track progress and provide timely alerts [^10.51593_20210064].                  
+                                                                                                              
+## Philosophical Perspectives                                                                                 
+                                                                                                              
+This contribution examines the intersection of human intelligence research, cognitive enhancements, and the   
philosophical movements of trans- and posthumanism. It discusses the promises and perils of developing an      
artificial "super-intelligence," outlining how psychology and individual differences should inform the         
development of such systems to ensure they align with human values and societal needs                          
[^10.1016_j.intell.2021.101563].                                                                               
                                                                                                               

